[Desktop Entry]
Type=Application
Name=Calculator
GenericName=Arithmetic
Comment=The shell's keypad, over the whole screen
# The CLI, not a window: this shell draws no windows of its own, so there is
# nothing here to exec directly. `banditshell calculator` asks the running shell
# over IPC to put its panel out, which is the same route the keybind takes.
#
# `app` AND NOT `toggle`, which is the difference between the two ways in.
# The key ($mod+K) opens the strip on the sidebar's flank, for the sum you do
# while something else has your attention. This is the entry somebody picked out
# of an application menu by NAME, which is a request for the application: the
# same calculator standing over the whole screen, with the keypad grown to suit
# it. modules/calculator/CalculatorPanel.qml is one object in two shapes, so
# whatever was on the line is still on it whichever route you came by.
#
# It is still a TOGGLE, so the entry behaves the way the key does: launching it
# twice puts the panel away, which is what everything else that summons a surface
# in this shell already contracts to (docs/hyprland-binds.example.conf says the
# same sentence about every bind in it). Launched while the flank panel is out it
# promotes that panel rather than closing it, because an entry reading
# "Calculator" must not answer a request for the calculator by hiding one.
Exec=banditshell calculator app
Icon=accessories-calculator
Terminal=false
# NoDisplay is deliberately off. The whole reason this file exists is that it
# lands in the launcher's own list, so the panel is reachable by typing its name
# as well as by the key, and by any other application menu on the machine.
Categories=Utility;Calculator;
Keywords=calculator;arithmetic;maths;math;
StartupNotify=false
